  "body": "## What happens\n\n`cargo test -p camcraft-app --test lead_approach` fails 2 tests on upstream/main b6c02115:\n\n- `the_reported_keep_down_helix_pocket_enters_every_level_once`\n- `the_horizontal_arc_entry_on_the_users_pocket_verifies_silent`\n\nBoth stop at line 108: `the stock-source pocket cuts the user's part: []`.\n\n## Cause\n\nCommit 086f4010 (#1603) made the helper `beside_the_cut_part` assert that the stock-source pocket on `Milling-test.step` cuts the part. At that time the pocket cut through the part.\n\nPR #1656 (#1554) merged at 12:16Z. It makes a stock-source pocket clear the stock around the part. So the pocket no longer cuts the part, and the assertion is now wrong. The new behaviour is correct.\n\n## Fix\n\nChange the helper to assert that the stock-source pocket has no `Gouge`. Keep the entry-law checks on the remaining warnings.\n\n## Done means\n\n`lead_approach` passes on main. The helper pins that the stock-source pocket stays off the part.\n",
